Z||000019||AusFiero||07-06-2001||02:59 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by b lo 0:<BR><B>To use an Australian term- CRIKEY!  Does making white-face gauges get you chicks?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Crikey is actually a Pommy word. We certainly don't use it much anymore. Think it was popular in the 50s and 60s. Fair Dinkum.<P>And LOL on the gauges comment. <P>Fieros are pretty rare in Australia and attract attention big time. Get lots of girls give a wave and a smile   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> So finding anyone willing to pose with it isn't really a problem. One girl at a bus stop once looked right through my wife basically and blew a big kiss. Wife just laughed at her. She thinks it is my mid life crisis car. lol<P>It's the same like that in America with Fieros isn't it ?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by AusFiero (edited 07-06-2001).]||||reg||1
