Z||000024||AusFiero||07-06-2001||11:46 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>I just think its only right that she gets some benefit out of it be diff if she was a gf. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>LOL SHHHHH Roger. Let my wife see things like that and she might make me get rid of my Fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>Bill I am 36 late this year. Haen't always had sports cars but have owned 46 cars to date. So I have sorta had a broad cross section. <P>The Fiero is the longest I have ever kept a car. 4 other cars have have parked next to it since I have had it. A family hack station wagon I was glad to get rid of, a Subaru WRX Turbo, awesome car but to small for the family, a Mitsubishi Magna Sports with a 5 speed semi automatic triptronic transmission and it currently resides with our 98 Holden Commodore R91 Police Pack. <P>Fieros must be special, it's still here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000025||mrgone||07-06-2001||11:52 AM||||semi automatic? <BR>ive seen this in rally video games but never knew what was the diff<P>im always going to have a sports car<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_9.jpg">   <BR><B>86.5 2m4 5speed turd 241,000kms</B>||||reg||1
Z||000026||AusFiero||07-07-2001||01:16 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrgone:<BR><B>semi automatic? <BR>ive seen this in rally video games but never knew what was the diff<P>im always going to have a sports car<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>A tiptronic transmission allows you to push the gear lever up and down 1 gate as a normal automatic. Flip the shifter to the right and it engages another gate. The car becomes semi automatic. Gearchanges up, push it forward, gearing down, pull it back. Makes for fast manual driving. Is same as the system used in some Porsche models. Originated from Formula 1 technology.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000027||The Fieromaster||07-09-2001||10:18 AM||||Aus... nice car... nice girls... but.. your sellin your ride?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      "Raced That Wrecked Better"<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">     <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>AIM: Fieromaster<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
Z||000028||AusFiero||07-09-2001||10:59 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by The Fieromaster:<BR><B>Aus... nice car... nice girls... but.. your sellin your ride?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah. I have an 88 with factory option t-tops sitting in storage for me to replace it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. Is already RHD, need restoration or in my case renovation and is only AU$6000 or about $3100 to $3200 US.<P>I want to build a radical custom next time around. Totally new interior style, radical body and an engine swap to yet be decided. Well it will be an Archie V8 kit probably. Well that is unless I figure out how to shoehorn one of the little turboed jap v8s available over into it.  They are pretty cheap motors in these parts.<P><BR>But in the meantime I have to rebuild the AusFiero before the car. Well I will let the surgeons do that rebuild I think.<BR>||||reg||1
